From: Hiroki Nakagawa <nhiroki@chromium.org>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 21:32:46 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 20/26] [M156] Prerender: Delete pending deletion subframe RFHs
 before activation

Differences from the pure cherry-pick:
- Explicitly enable `blink::features::kPrerender2CrossOriginIframes`
  via `ScopedFeatureList` in
  `PrerenderPendingDeletionSubframeBrowserTest`. This feature was
  enabled by default in M159 (https://crrev.com/c/8673922) and is
  disabled by default prior to M159, causing cross-origin subframe
  navigations during prerendering in the new test to be deferred and
  time out.
- Production code (`prerender_host.cc`) is unchanged.

Original change's description:
> Prerender: Delete pending deletion subframe RFHs before activation
>
> On prerender activation, PrerenderHost::Activate() moves the subframe
> FrameTreeNodes of the prerendered page to the primary FrameTree, and
> updates the FrameTree of their current and speculative
> RenderFrameHosts. However, the RenderFrameHosts in the subframes'
> pending deletion lists (i.e., the ones swapped out on navigation and
> still waiting for unload completion) were moved along with the
> FrameTreeNodes without having their FrameTree updated. They kept
> pointing to the prerendering FrameTree, which is destroyed during
> activation, while they could still receive messages from the renderer
> until the unload ACK or timeout, resulting in a use-after-free.
>
> This CL deletes the RenderFrameHosts in the subframes' pending
> deletion lists before activation, as if their unload timeout expired.
> This is consistent with those in the main frame's pending deletion
> list, which are deleted when the prerendering FrameTree is shut down.
>
